# Security reviews

[docs/security-review.md](docs/security-review.md) is the **single source of truth**. Read it before any security audit or before changing authz, mmctl/password, audit KV, ScopeConfig, slash commands, or `.github/workflows/`.

## Do

- Start at the coverage map; pick the **oldest** surface. Do not re-read `checker.go` by default.
- Diff the change against **Controls in force**. New route / mutator / KV write / workflow step needs a named guard, proof class (`host` | `lab` | `manual`), and a proof of that class.
- Apply the **false-green rule**: stubbed `changePassword` and in-memory `memKV` prove logic only, not live mmctl or plugin KV.
- State what you **disproved**, not only what you found. Cite `file:line`.
- Same PR: bump coverage-map dates, move closed rows to Resolved, append **Audit history**.

## Do not

- Reopen [Accepted residuals](docs/security-review.md#accepted-residuals) or the Resolved table without **new evidence**.
- Re-file CodeQL `actions/unpinned-tag` (fleet won't-fix). `@main` on `plugin-ci.yml` is **R1**, not that residual.
- Treat organizer-intended powers (in-scope create/reset) as findings.
- Cite Z3 `proof_username_whitelist.py` as “injection impossible” — alphabet only (**V2**).

Findings use ledger IDs (`R2`, `V1`, `S1`, `I2`, `R1`, `C1`, `P1`). Operator claims: [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).
